Z||000000||jimmybpei||09-16-2001||05:48 PM||||Has anyone done the yet.<P>Looking for the easiest connections posssible<BR>to the c203 plug. think i have found allthe wires i need on the caddy but where do they go. can you tell me ex: blu/whit caddy to red/wite fiero c203<P>my car is a 86 se 4cyl with no options also <BR>5 speed izuzu.<P>bubbajoexx site is very good but could be a litte more through in this area rather than just labeling each wire.<P>this is not quite enough explanation for the lay person. concect A to B is what i'm looking for here as im sure alot more people <BR>out there would like as well <P>Thankx<BR>Jimmy B.||||reg||5
Z||000001||KRMFiero||09-16-2001||07:55 PM||||e-mail me and I'll try my best to explain what wires go where, also are you using Fiero Tranny or Caddy?<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 V-8/Overdrive Tranny<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White) 5 speed with blown clutch :(<P>         <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg">   <BR>AOL: Physcokyle     AGE: 15||||reg||1
Z||000002||jelly2m8||09-16-2001||08:11 PM||||Hey jimmy, <P> Which intake setup are you using, MPI, or carbed?.<P> If its carbed, use the Fiero wiring harness, and make the changes to the engine end of the harness. <P>If its a MPI motor, you will use the caddy harness, and make the changes to the connectors. The best way to figgure out which wire goes where is to get helms manual for both the fiero, and the helms for the donor car. Then you can look at the wiring diagrams to see which wire goes to which pin out.<P> Most Gm dealers will loan you these manuals.<BR>If you need I can help you with the Fiero diagrams||||reg||1
